{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310774,"nonce":"hnafRPq38amJxf/BNKG+xv0jJa4=","title":"Frozen archive of compiler features shipped 2026-02-10 to 2026-03-10 (Haxe macro system, enum abstract, Array methods, @:from/@:to, object ...","message":"This archive freezes the \"Features Implemented\" section that used to live\ninline in MEMORY.md. Each entry has the canonical _what / key files / key\ninsights_ shape from the older session-notes format. None of these features\nhave regressed; they're load-bearing in current code.\n\n**What**: Complete macro expansion pipeline with aggressive performance optimizations.\n**Key files**: `compiler/src/macro_system/` (11 modules: expander, interpreter, registry, value, ast_bridge, environment, reification, build_macros, context_api, errors, mod).\n**Pipeline**: Parse → `expand_macros()` → TAST lowering. Macros are expanded BETWEEN parsing and type checking.\n**Macro types**: Functions use `haxe.macro.Expr` param/return types. Macro definitions are stripped from output AST before TAST lowering (their types don't exist in runtime type system).\n**Key insight — Expr unwrapping**: Macro params arrive as `MacroValue::Expr(AST_node)`. `unwrap_expr_value()` extracts concrete values (Int, Float, String, etc.) from literal AST nodes. Called automatically in `apply_binary_op`, `is_truthy`, `as_int`, `as_float`.\n**Key insight — array push mutation**: `array.push()` returns NEW array (immutable values). Must update variable in-place via `env.set()` when base is an Ident.\n**Performance optimizations**: (1) Arc-based MacroValue (O(1) clone), (2) Selective closure capture (only captures referenced vars), (3) Memoization cache for identical macro calls, (4) Dirty set tracking (iteration 2+ only re-expands changed declarations).\n**E2E verified**: `compileTimeAdd(100,200)→300`, `doubled(21)→42`, `makeGreeting(\"World\")→\"Hello, World!\"`, `fibonacci(10)→55`, `generateSquares(5)→[0,1,4,9,16]`, `#if rayzor`→works.\n\n**What**: `enum abstract Color(Int) { var Red = 0; var Green = 1; }` — named static constants backed by underlying type.\n**Key files**: `parser/src/haxe_ast.rs` (`is_enum_abstract` field), `compiler/src/tast/node.rs` (TypedAbstract), `compiler/src/tast/ast_lowering.rs` (class_fields registration + SymbolKind::Abstract handler), `compiler/src/ir/tast_to_hir.rs` (evaluate_inline_static_vars + StaticFieldAccess).\n**Key insight — inline_var_values reuse**: Enum abstract fields are treated as `static inline var` constants. `evaluate_inline_static_vars()` scans `file.abstracts` alongside `file.classes` to pre-evaluate them. The `StaticFieldAccess` handler checks `inline_var_values` first (covers abstracts) before searching class fields.\n**Key insight — StaticFieldAccess must check inline_var_values**: The fallback path `StaticFieldAccess → HirExprKind::Variable` does NOT hit the `TypedExpressionKind::Variable` handler (which checks `inline_var_values`), because it produces an HIR expression directly. The fix: check `inline_var_values` at the TOP of the `StaticFieldAccess` handler.\n**Key insight — class_fields needed for abstracts**: Abstract field access resolution (`Color.Red`) requires the abstract's SymbolId in `class_fields` map. Added `class_fields.insert(abstract_symbol, Vec::new())` before processing abstract fields.\n\n**What**: Implemented 9 missing Array methods: indexOf, lastIndexOf, contains, concat, splice, shift, unshift, resize, toString.\n**Key files**: `runtime/src/haxe_array.rs` (runtime functions), `compiler/src/stdlib/array.rs` (MIR wrappers), `compiler/src/stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs` (stdlib mappings), `runtime/src/plugin_impl.rs` (symbol registration).\n**Critical insight — shift/pop need boxed return**: Methods returning `Null\u003cT\u003e` (shift, pop) MUST return boxed DynamicValue* (via `_ptr` variant), NOT raw i64, because `trace()` dereferences the return as a DynamicValue pointer. Raw i64 causes SIGSEGV.\n**Critical insight — optional params need MIR wrappers**: `indexOf(x, ?fromIndex)` has optional param. Direct mapping to 3-arg runtime function fails because compiler only passes 2 args. Solution: MIR wrapper defaults the optional param (e.g., `array_index_of(arr, value)` calls `haxe_array_index_of(arr, value, 0)`).\n**E2E**: 10/10 tests in `test_array_methods_e2e.rs`.\n\n**What**: General mechanism for `@:from`/`@:to` metadata on abstract static methods. Replaces hardcoded SIMD4f path.\n**Key files**: `tast_to_hir.rs` (scan methods for metadata), `hir_to_mir.rs` (rule storage + Cast/Let/Assign handlers), `ast_lowering.rs` (TAST implicit cast for array/object literals).\n**Critical insight — name-based keying**: HIR and type_table create DIFFERENT SymbolIds and TypeIds for the same abstract. The only stable identifier is the abstract's `qualified_name` (or `native_name` for extern abstracts like SIMD4f). Rules are keyed by `InternedString` name, not TypeId or SymbolId.\n**Lookup chain**: `resolve_abstract_name()` gets TypeId → TypeKind::Abstract → symbol_id → symbol → `qualified_name.or(native_name).or(name)`.\n**Rule storage**: `abstract_from_rules: BTreeMap\u003cInternedString, Vec\u003cHirCastRule\u003e\u003e` on HirToMirContext.\n**Three entry points for @:from**: (1) Cast handler (`try_abstract_from_cast`), (2) Let handler (`maybe_abstract_from_convert`), (3) Assign handler (`maybe_abstract_from_convert`).\n\n**What**: Every class allocation prepends `__type_id: i64` at GEP index 0. Enables runtime type identification.\n**Key files**: `hir_to_mir.rs` (register_class_metadata field_index starts at 1, New handler stores type_id), `runtime/src/type_system.rs` (haxe_object_get_type_id, haxe_object_is_instance), `scalar_replacement.rs` (skip field_idx == 0).\n**Type.getClass()**: Maps to `haxe_object_get_type_id` via stdlib mapping. Reads first 8 bytes of object pointer.\n**SRA compatibility**: SRA skips GEP index 0 (header field) to avoid type conflicts with user fields.\n\n**What**: `Null\u003cInt\u003e`, `Null\u003cFloat\u003e`, `Null\u003cBool\u003e` — box primitives as `DynamicValue*` to distinguish null from 0/0.0/false.\n**Key files**: `ast_lowering.rs` (Null\u003cT\u003e→Optional), `hir_to_mir.rs` (convert_type, maybe_box_for_optional, lower_null_coalesce), `tast_to_hir.rs` (?? NullCoalesce passthrough), `builder.rs` (IrValue::Null type fix).\n**Key insight — ?? desugaring path**: `??` is desugared to `HirExprKind::If` in tast_to_hir.rs (line ~1796), NOT through `HirBinaryOp::NullCoalesce`. For Optional{primitive} LHS, must bypass desugar and emit `NullCoalesce` so MIR handler unboxes in pass-through block.\n**Key insight — IrValue::Null register type**: `build_const(IrValue::Null)` fell into `_ =\u003e IrType::Any` wildcard, causing `maybe_box_for_optional` to miss the Ptr(_) check. Fix: explicit `IrValue::Null =\u003e IrType::Ptr(Box::new(IrType::Void))`.\n**Key insight — null literal boxing**: Null assigned to `Null\u003cT\u003e` must stay as null pointer (Ptr(Void)), NOT be boxed via `haxe_box_int_ptr(0)`. The `maybe_box_for_optional` Ptr check handles this once IrValue::Null has correct register type.\n\n**What**: `obj?.field`, `obj?.method()`, `a?.b?.c` — desugared at TAST→HIR to `if (obj != null) obj.field else null`.\n**Key files**: `tast_to_hir.rs` (FieldAccess/MethodCall desugaring), `hir_to_mir.rs` (lower_conditional handles it).\n**Key insight — double evaluation**: Complex expressions (non-Variable) need Let binding to avoid evaluating twice. Simple Variable objects use clone.\n\n**What**: Generic class methods (e.g., BalancedTree.setLoop, compare) that inherit type params from the enclosing class are now transitively monomorphized.\n**Key files**: `compiler/src/ir/monomorphize.rs` (Phase 6: `propagate_transitive_fixups`, `instantiate_with_sub_map`).\n**Key insight — transitive closure**: `funcs_with_fixups` must include NOT just functions with direct `type_param_tag_fixups`, but also functions that transitively CALL functions with fixups. E.g., if `compare()` has fixups and `setLoop()` calls `compare()`, `setLoop` must be in the set too.\n**Key insight — cache hit overwrite bug**: `instantiate_with_sub_map` returns `(IrFunctionId, bool)` where bool indicates if newly created. On cache hits, do NOT insert into module (dummy clone would overwrite correctly specialized function).\n**Key insight — sub_map storage**: `instantiation_sub_maps: HashMap\u003cIrFunctionId, HashMap\u003cString, IrType\u003e\u003e` stores substitution maps for each specialized function, enabling transitive propagation.\n\n**What**: `function new(l, k, v, r, h = -1)` — calling with fewer args fills defaults from HIR param defaults.\n**Key files**: `hir_to_mir.rs` (`function_param_defaults` map, `fill_default_args` helper, 4 call site instrumentations).\n\n**What**: `extern public inline function get_height():Int return this == null ? 0 : _height;` — inline method that safely handles null receiver.\n**Key insight — this == null comparison**: Class pointer types (`TreeNode`) and Dynamic both lower to `Ptr(Void)` in MIR. The Dynamic BinaryOp handler checked MIR `Ptr(Void)`, incorrectly treating class pointers as Dynamic. Fix: check actual HIR `TypeKind::Dynamic` instead of MIR type.\n**Key insight — extern inline just works**: `extern` + `inline` functions already have their body lowered normally. The `inline` modifier sets `InlineHint::Always`. No special extern handling needed for the body. Return type annotation required.\n\n**What**: `var p:{x:Int,y:Int} = new Point(3,7)` and `var narrow:{x:Int,y:Int} = wideAnon` — deferred wrapping approach.\n**Key files**: `hir_to_mir.rs` (AnonBacking enum, anon_views map, try_register_anon_view, materialize_anon_view, materialize_class_to_anon, materialize_wider_anon_to_anon), `type_checker.rs` (Anonymous←Anonymous width subtyping, Anonymous←Class).\n**Architecture — deferred wrap**: Keep original value (class pointer or wider anon handle), redirect field access at compile time. Only materialize a real AnonObject at escape points (function call args, return).\n**Key insight — sorted-index mismatch**: Anonymous fields accessed by alphabetically-sorted index. Field `y` is index 1 in `{x,y,z}` but index 0 in `{y,z}`. WiderAnon backing remaps indices.\n**Key insight — Class backing**: Class→anon uses GEP+Load with class field_index_map, no allocation for local access. Preserves reference semantics (class mutation visible through anon view).\n**Key insight — call boundary materialization**: `maybe_materialize_for_call` uses `function_param_hir_types` to detect when callee expects anon but arg is class/wider-anon. Creates real AnonObject via rayzor_anon_new + field copying.\n**Three materialization paths**: (1) Variable with anon_views entry, (2) Direct class→anon at call boundary, (3) Direct wider-anon→anon at call boundary.\n\n**What**: `Future.create(() -\u003e expr)` creates lazy future, `.await()` spawns + blocks, `.then(cb)` non-blocking, `.poll()`, `.isReady()`, `.awaitTimeout(ms)`, `.cancel()`, `Future.all()`, `Future.race()`.\n**Key files**: `runtime/src/future.rs` (FutureHandle + 12 extern fns), `compiler/src/stdlib/future.rs` (MIR wrappers), `compiler/src/stdlib/runtime_mapping.rs` (11 map_method!), `compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/concurrent/Future.hx` (extern class).\n**Send/Sync**: `core_types.rs` has `is_future()` + `get_future_create_closure()`. `send_sync_validator.rs` validates Future.create() closures same as Thread.spawn().\n**Key insight — JIT closure returns i64**: Changed from i32 to i64 to prevent 64-bit pointer truncation for String/object/array-returning futures.\n**Key insight — catch_unwind + setjmp**: Worker threads use `catch_unwind` (Rust panics) + `_setjmp`/exception handler (Haxe exceptions). Both paths store error in FutureHandle, `.await()` re-throws via `rayzor_throw_typed`. ACTIVE_THREAD_COUNT always decremented.\n**Key insight — jit_cleanup after wait_all_threads**: `call_main()` must call `rayzor_jit_cleanup()` after `rayzor_wait_all_threads()` to reset ACTIVE_THREAD_COUNT between test runs.\n**Key insight — MakeClosure register type**: `build_make_closure` must call `set_register_type(dest, Ptr(U8))`. Without this, closure registers default to I64, causing `maybe_box_for_extern_call` to box closure pointers via `haxe_box_int_ptr` → corrupted fn_ptr.\n**Key insight — Function type in is_type_erased_ptr**: `TypeKind::Function` must be in the `is_type_erased_ptr` match list (hir_to_mir.rs ~line 10225). Closure pointers stored as I64 are type-erased pointers, should be CAST not BOXED.\n**Future.join()**: Static method calling `rayzor_wait_all_threads()`. Blocks until all futures/threads complete.\n**Future.all(arr)**: Returns a lazy Future resolving to Array of results. Uses custom thread spawn (not `spawn_future`) to store full 64-bit Array* result. `raw_result: bool` flag on FutureHandle skips int-boxing in `rayzor_future_await`.\n\n**What**: `@:async static function compute(x:Int):Int { return x*2; }` → calling `compute(21)` returns lazy Future handle, `.await()` blocks.\n**Key files**: `tast/symbols.rs` (ASYNC flag bit 19), `tast/ast_lowering.rs` (@:async metadata parsing), `ir/hir.rs` (is_async on HirFunction), `ir/tast_to_hir.rs` (propagate is_async), `ir/hir_to_mir.rs` (lower_async_function_body + ensure_future_externs + async dispatch).\n**Architecture**: (1) `lower_async_function_body` splits function: inner closure via `generate_lambda_skeleton`, outer function creates MakeClosure → Load fn_ptr/env_ptr → call `rayzor_future_create`. (2) `async_result_registers: BTreeSet\u003cIrId\u003e` tracks Future handles. (3) `.await()` dispatch in Call handler intercepts method calls on tracked registers.\n**Key insight — ClosureFunc/ClosureEnv broken for extraction**: `ClosureFunc` returns closure object ptr (not fn_ptr), `ClosureEnv` returns current function's env param. Must use Load at offset 0 (fn_ptr) and PtrAdd+Load at offset 8 (env_ptr) from MakeClosure result instead.\n**Key insight — stdlib functions not available during MIR lowering**: `ensure_future_externs()` declares `rayzor_future_create/await/poll/is_ready` as IrExternFunction directly in the user module since stdlib is merged AFTER MIR lowering.\n**Key insight — async detection for StaticMethodCall**: Let handler's async check must handle both `Variable(symbol)` and `Field { field: method_symbol }` callee patterns since `tast_to_hir` wraps StaticMethodCall as Field.\n**Key insight — MethodCall pattern**: `.await()` becomes `Call { callee: Variable(method_sym), args: [receiver, ...], is_method: true }` — receiver is args[0], NOT in the callee Field pattern.\n**Key insight — type_checking_pipeline Await todo**: Replaced `todo!()` with `self.check_expression(expression)?; return Ok(*await_type);`.\n\n**What**: `e.stack` populated at throw time with source-mapped call stack. `e.details()` returns message + trace. Debug/release mode gating.\n**Key files**: `hir_to_mir.rs` (Throw handler ~line 4110), `Exception.hx` (stack field), `native_stack_trace.rs` (capture), `panic_guard.rs` (flag-gated guarded_call).\n**Key insight — GEP element type for struct fields**: GEP with `Ptr(U8)` element type uses `elem_size=1` in cranelift backend. For struct field stores, must use `Ptr(Void)` to get `elem_size=8`. Using wrong type causes byte-offset GEP instead of field-offset GEP.\n**Key insight — static call via Field callee**: `tast_to_hir.rs` wraps `StaticMethodCall` as `Field { object: class_symbol, field: method_symbol }` for disambiguation. The MIR lowerer's Field callee path passes the object as `this`. For static calls, the object is a class reference (not instance) — must detect via SymbolKind and skip passing it as `this`. Fix at ~line 7809.\n**Debug vs Release**: `guarded_call` checks `is_enabled()` — release mode calls closure directly (zero overhead), debug mode wraps with `catch_unwind`.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `features_implemented_archive` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}